 back and forth across an item is instant after the first visit.
 
@@ -503,6 +509,12 @@ number clustering has to beat to be worth anything.
 Answers are cached against the prompt text, so re-running an unchanged case is free and
 editing a prompt invalidates exactly the answers it affects.
 
+An answer is only cached once the caller has accepted it. Schema-valid is not the same as
+usable: a clustering that organised nothing parses perfectly, and caching it meant replaying
+a known-bad result on every open until someone refreshed by hand. A cached answer is judged
+by the same standard when it is read back, so entries stored before a caller learned to
+reject them are forgotten and asked again rather than served forever.
+
 At the time of writing, over two fixtures: grouping 95.5% against a 87.7% heuristic
 baseline, order 90.8% against 85.1%. On the small, clean case the model is perfect on both.
